# Screen Review Checklist

Before completing a new or modified screen, review the following.

## Design
- [ ] Uses the existing design tokens, fonts, theme, and shared components.
- [ ] Has a clear visual hierarchy and an intentional layout.
- [ ] Avoids unnecessary cards, decoration, and duplicated navigation chrome.
- [ ] Uses consistent spacing, typography, alignment, and touch targets.
- [ ] Includes relevant loading, empty, error, and success states.

## Layout
- [ ] Respects top and bottom safe areas.
- [ ] Does not apply the same inset twice.
- [ ] Does not overlap the status bar, tab bar, or home indicator.
- [ ] Handles keyboard interactions where relevant.
- [ ] Works with long content and localized text.
- [ ] Avoids arbitrary fixed screen dimensions.
- [ ] Supports RTL according to the project's existing strategy.

## Implementation
- [ ] Reuses existing components and Expo Router conventions.
- [ ] Uses APIs compatible with installed package versions.
- [ ] Uses Reanimated appropriately.
- [ ] Uses an appropriate list implementation for the dataset size.
- [ ] Has no known type errors, broken imports, or missing keys.
- [ ] Preserves existing behavior.

## Verification
- [ ] Run available type checks and linting.
- [ ] Inspect the running application when tooling permits.
- [ ] Check a narrow layout and a larger layout where practical.
- [ ] Check keyboard, safe-area, and navigation interactions where relevant.
- [ ] Record anything that could not be tested.

Source-code review alone does not prove that a screen renders correctly. Report unresolved issues honestly.